From 812b6eaa684e3bf3849131a1dd15fea4906d2750 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <devnull@projectluma.local>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 18:26:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] headerbar: complete the generic Luma application frame

Resolve the compatibility identity through GDesktopAppInfo (localized name and
registered icon, with window/default icon names, the application-ID icon, and
the generic executable icon as ordered fallbacks), clip tile icons to the 6px
identity radius, and hide a synthesized title that repeats the identity.

A GtkHeaderBar that is the titlebar (or the leading child of the vertical box
content) of a generic application window and owns the automatic identity keeps
the clean 42px title row and re-hosts its packed start/end children on the
Luma command row directly below; pack/remove keep routing there, the
default-decoration heuristic sees the re-hosted children, and the
luma-no-command-row escape class opts out. The work surface owns its rounded
clip and begins 9px below the title row, or flush under a command row.
libadwaita windows (luma-adw-native-window) mark their own content, so GTK no
longer marks their internal dialog host. The theme pins the 24px connected
control pill, the command-group geometry, the identity spacing, and stable
backdrop chrome for generic windows in both the maintained SCSS and the
generated release CSS.
